WEBVTT

00:31.114 --> 00:33.950
THE TRUNK

01:01.561 --> 01:06.107
The person you are calling
is currently unavailable. Please leave…

01:09.027 --> 01:11.821
At least come up with a reasonable excuse
before you go!

01:12.906 --> 01:14.157
Otherwise, it's all over.

01:15.033 --> 01:15.867
Move aside.

01:16.993 --> 01:19.329
I don't have time
to talk to a nobody like you.

03:39.510 --> 03:40.637
Just say something.

03:41.221 --> 03:43.056
Whether it's an excuse or a confession.

03:45.016 --> 03:46.351
Is that what she told you?

03:48.853 --> 03:50.313
That I had cameras installed?

03:53.942 --> 03:54.943
She's right. I did.

03:56.194 --> 03:58.571
Am I not allowed
to watch you go about your day?

04:00.490 --> 04:02.116
I would've gone crazy otherwise.

04:02.617 --> 04:05.119
I had to see for myself
that you still longed for me,

04:05.203 --> 04:06.496
even with her by your side.

04:08.039 --> 04:10.750
That was the only way
I could think of taking you back.

04:17.674 --> 04:19.259
Are you telling me you did this

04:20.593 --> 04:22.220
so you could come back to me?

04:23.805 --> 04:26.349
As I was entering the operating room…

04:28.434 --> 04:30.395
you begged them to save the baby over me.

04:32.355 --> 04:33.606
How could you do that?

04:34.899 --> 04:36.818
How could Han Jeong-won do that to me?

04:38.278 --> 04:40.405
I saw you step into the road that day.

04:42.448 --> 04:44.617
I was angry
and blamed you for what happened.

04:46.953 --> 04:48.204
I pitied

04:49.372 --> 04:50.415
our baby.

04:55.753 --> 04:57.463
I was trying to die with it.

04:58.756 --> 05:01.676
After I got pregnant,
every day was a living hell.

05:03.011 --> 05:05.930
It felt like I'd become
the most useless person on earth.

05:06.973 --> 05:10.435
I was withering away,
dreading having to give birth,

05:10.518 --> 05:11.352
but you!

05:12.770 --> 05:15.857
You seemed thrilled,
like the baby breathed new life into you.

05:17.400 --> 05:18.651
Do you know how it feels

05:18.735 --> 05:20.862
to be reduced to nothing more

05:21.738 --> 05:22.989
than wrapping paper?

05:23.072 --> 05:24.949
You should have told me!

05:25.450 --> 05:27.285
You should have told me you weren't ready.

05:27.785 --> 05:30.913
And have to bear your disappointed face?

05:32.332 --> 05:34.959
Apparently, mothers put
their babies' safety first.

05:35.918 --> 05:37.670
I was disgusted with myself too.

05:40.298 --> 05:42.717
But I can't change
my lack of maternal instincts.

05:53.436 --> 05:56.689
I'm to blame for not realizing sooner
how much pain you were in.

05:58.566 --> 06:01.027
I was the fool, the idiot,
and the son of a bitch.

06:01.986 --> 06:03.154
That's how I found closure.

06:04.030 --> 06:07.867
I thought we could move past all this
if we just got together again.

06:09.786 --> 06:11.037
But how could you

06:12.497 --> 06:14.540
do exactly what my father did to me?

06:16.709 --> 06:18.461
I was scared. What else could I do?

06:21.130 --> 06:23.424
I had no other way to hold on to you.

06:25.885 --> 06:26.719
Jeong-won.

06:28.429 --> 06:29.847
We're accomplices, remember?

06:31.474 --> 06:32.892
I killed the baby,

06:33.393 --> 06:34.852
and you killed your mother.

06:36.229 --> 06:39.107
If that makes us sinners,
we can atone together.

06:39.774 --> 06:41.484
You and I, together.

06:51.577 --> 06:52.745
You're insane.

06:54.789 --> 06:55.957
I'll atone for my sins.

06:58.543 --> 07:00.628
But I won't be doing so by your side.

08:27.006 --> 08:28.216
Should we go on a trip?

09:34.782 --> 09:37.618
Why didn't you tell me
about the hidden camera?

09:41.038 --> 09:43.291
I didn't know how.

09:44.208 --> 09:46.711
I should have handled it
before you found out.

09:48.671 --> 09:50.339
I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

09:51.132 --> 09:52.508
That sounds like an excuse.

09:53.884 --> 09:57.305
I bet you just turned a blind eye
to avoid problems in this marriage.

09:58.347 --> 09:59.890
I didn't turn a blind eye.

10:01.767 --> 10:04.729
I grabbed Ms. Lee Seo-yeon by the hair
and even beat her up a little.

10:05.813 --> 10:07.690
You hit Lee Seo-yeon?

10:08.316 --> 10:09.275
Almost killed her.

10:10.484 --> 10:12.236
Those blue pills taped to that LP…

10:13.654 --> 10:15.531
I found out what they were.

10:16.282 --> 10:18.367
And before I knew it, I was furious.

10:19.744 --> 10:22.663
If I'd put my mind to it,
I could have broken a rib or two.

10:23.706 --> 10:25.958
Didn't I mention that I learned jujitsu?

10:28.461 --> 10:29.920
I wish I'd been there to see it.

10:31.589 --> 10:33.215
Whose side would you have taken?

10:58.658 --> 11:00.159
You actually hit Lee Seo-yeon?

11:02.203 --> 11:04.997
You seriously pulled out her hair?

11:32.525 --> 11:33.859
It's a family.

11:44.829 --> 11:46.706
Let's get groceries together sometime.

11:47.957 --> 11:50.418
We'll grab beer
and ingredients for a few side dishes.

11:50.918 --> 11:52.586
We'll push the cart together,

11:53.546 --> 11:55.047
and say things like,

11:55.131 --> 11:57.717
"That's too much."
"That milk tastes better."

12:01.470 --> 12:02.805
What's your favorite dish?

12:06.350 --> 12:07.768
I'd like to cook it for you.

12:15.860 --> 12:17.737
How long will you live in that house?

12:20.448 --> 12:21.449
If I were you…

12:28.205 --> 12:29.039
Let's get going.

12:37.339 --> 12:40.384
What was that? "If I were you," what?

12:43.095 --> 12:45.556
That's an odd habit,
bailing before the punchline.

12:48.017 --> 12:48.851
What is it?

12:51.437 --> 12:52.313
Tell me.

14:36.166 --> 14:38.002
Your hands are cold. Just hold on.

14:42.298 --> 14:43.966
I recognized you from the start.

14:46.844 --> 14:48.178
I'm Mr. Han Jeong-won's wife.

14:56.687 --> 14:58.355
All right, look this way, please.

14:59.064 --> 15:00.941
One, two…

15:02.610 --> 15:05.404
At the columbarium,
and then the graduation ceremony…

15:07.781 --> 15:09.825
It was a pretty rough day,

15:11.327 --> 15:15.372
but it felt like you were the one person
in the universe who could understand me.

15:16.999 --> 15:18.834
Had I gotten to know you back then…

15:21.837 --> 15:24.548
I wonder how things might have been
if we'd met sooner.

15:28.427 --> 15:32.640
It's possible that our relationship
might not have lasted long.

15:33.766 --> 15:34.600
But…

15:38.520 --> 15:42.191
I think I'd have recognized you
even if I'd passed you by a hundred times.

15:50.783 --> 15:52.326
I really like you.

15:53.577 --> 15:55.162
I want to be with you all the time.

16:14.014 --> 16:14.890
Let's get divorced.

16:19.520 --> 16:21.271
I brought you here to end things.

16:24.441 --> 16:27.277
Did I do something wrong?

16:27.778 --> 16:29.780
Tell me what the issue is.

16:31.532 --> 16:33.575
This marriage is a failed marriage.

16:35.744 --> 16:37.955
It's my fault. I crossed the line.

16:38.831 --> 16:44.169
I no longer have a reason
to keep doing this, so

16:45.713 --> 16:46.714
I intend to stop.

16:51.844 --> 16:53.262
Let's stop with the lies.

16:54.054 --> 16:57.766
Acting like you're cold and bulletproof,
and that damn manual of yours.

16:58.392 --> 17:01.562
Deep down, haven't you longed
for something to hold on to?

17:03.397 --> 17:05.899
Isn't that why you clung
to these marriages?

17:05.983 --> 17:07.943
So you could live?

17:08.027 --> 17:11.280
Just admit that you and I
are both fragile, broken wrecks.

17:12.448 --> 17:15.242
Stop talking about goddamn lines…

17:20.831 --> 17:22.291
and just admit the truth.

17:26.462 --> 17:28.297
Admit that you've fallen for me too.

17:40.893 --> 17:42.644
I may have said I crossed a line,

17:43.937 --> 17:47.274
but don't take that to mean
you're someone special to me.

17:54.823 --> 17:56.909
This marriage is over, Mr. Han Jeong-won.

18:33.153 --> 18:35.864
I wonder how things might have been
if we'd met sooner.

18:37.407 --> 18:39.409
Had I gotten to know you back then…

18:41.161 --> 18:44.748
I think I'd have recognized you
even if I'd passed you by a hundred times.

18:45.791 --> 18:50.504
Come to think of it, you have a knack
for making those around you miserable.

18:52.256 --> 18:55.217
I wonder if you'd look my way
if I killed Han Jeong-won too.

18:55.717 --> 18:57.010
Why haven't you told him?

18:57.719 --> 19:00.639
Don't get me wrong.
It wasn't out of consideration for you.

19:00.722 --> 19:03.225
I guess
you don't want to see him get hurt.

19:04.852 --> 19:06.687
That doesn't make you any less fake.

19:29.501 --> 19:32.379
Are you really giving me this?
Why are you quitting?

19:33.046 --> 19:35.674
Thank you for always opening early for me.

19:35.757 --> 19:38.427
Feel free to come back whenever.
Maybe when it gets warmer.

19:39.303 --> 19:40.137
No.

19:41.513 --> 19:42.848
I probably won't be back.

19:57.988 --> 20:00.449
Are you in there? Ms. Noh In-ji.

20:01.241 --> 20:02.075
Ms. Noh In-ji!

20:03.577 --> 20:04.494
What a ruckus.

20:06.413 --> 20:07.497
Her latest dispatch?

20:17.466 --> 20:18.592
Hold this.

20:27.226 --> 20:28.060
Come on in.

20:34.066 --> 20:35.442
You can keep your shoes on.

20:59.675 --> 21:00.509
Thank you.

21:03.762 --> 21:04.846
You look decent.

21:07.975 --> 21:10.811
You don't know who I am, so why would you…

21:11.561 --> 21:14.398
You must have come all the way here
because you miss her.

21:18.735 --> 21:20.112
Where is Ms. In-ji?

21:21.989 --> 21:23.699
You should know, not me.

21:24.950 --> 21:25.909
Aren't you guys married?

21:26.410 --> 21:28.870
I'm sure she's somewhere
worrying about you too.

21:31.623 --> 21:35.585
Find her yourself now that things are over
with the guy who owns this place.

21:39.089 --> 21:40.173
Thanks for the drink.

21:58.984 --> 21:59.943
How adorable.

22:01.236 --> 22:03.447
- Could we pick up the pace a bit?
- Of course.

22:03.530 --> 22:06.325
- Please get rid of the chandelier quickly.
- Yes, of course.

22:06.825 --> 22:08.869
- Thank you for your work.
- I'll get that done now.

22:49.951 --> 22:53.830
She said she's quitting
and even gave me her paddles.

22:56.750 --> 22:58.960
Could you please call me
if she ever comes back?

23:05.300 --> 23:06.385
Sure.

23:26.571 --> 23:28.573
NM LEE SEON

23:30.784 --> 23:31.618
Hello?

23:32.119 --> 23:32.994
This is Lee Seon.

23:33.537 --> 23:36.039
I'm sorry your contract
was unexpectedly cut short.

23:36.832 --> 23:41.670
We're willing to pay a penalty
for the breach at your request.

23:42.462 --> 23:45.090
No, I have no intention of doing that.

23:46.341 --> 23:48.969
Please just make sure
Ms. Noh In-ji comes to no harm.

23:50.387 --> 23:52.806
Okay. I'll make sure of that.

23:54.891 --> 23:57.018
I still had things to say to her.

23:57.936 --> 24:01.106
There's so much I don't know.
If there's any way to contact her…

24:03.900 --> 24:05.444
please tell me.

24:07.571 --> 24:09.531
Now that the contract is terminated,

24:09.614 --> 24:12.075
I'm afraid I can't give you
any more information.

24:12.701 --> 24:13.577
I'm sorry.

24:34.639 --> 24:37.851
He won't be seeking any damages
for breach of contract,

24:38.351 --> 24:39.519
which is a relief.

24:39.603 --> 24:41.730
Please protect Mr. Han Jeong-won.

24:43.356 --> 24:47.402
Even if it goes against
what's best for NM.

24:49.029 --> 24:50.447
You two sure are strange.

24:51.031 --> 24:54.534
The contract expired,
yet you still try to protect each other.

24:58.747 --> 24:59.581
I'll be off now.

25:01.374 --> 25:03.251
Around two years into my marriage,

25:04.669 --> 25:06.338
I almost killed my husband.

25:11.384 --> 25:15.305
Marriages are purer
when they're a business transaction.

25:18.808 --> 25:22.020
Do you love Mr. Han Jeong-won?

25:24.689 --> 25:25.524
Are you scared?

25:27.025 --> 25:29.194
So much so
that you have to end things so abruptly?

25:53.760 --> 25:56.471
Seeing you here really makes it feel
like we're coworkers.

25:56.972 --> 26:00.100
Want to join me for a small farewell party
for us failed exes?

26:03.311 --> 26:04.896
I happened to like my marriage.

26:05.772 --> 26:08.316
Thanks to you,
it's become a blemish on my career.

26:08.817 --> 26:10.151
Even the CEO wants to see me.

26:34.217 --> 26:35.385
Hello?

26:35.468 --> 26:37.846
Finally. Why did you have
your phone turned off?

26:40.640 --> 26:45.645
This thing's harder to open
than I thought.

26:46.396 --> 26:49.941
It has a double lock,
so I need two sets of combinations.

26:50.650 --> 26:51.776
It must be quite pricey,

26:53.528 --> 26:54.362
this trunk.

26:55.780 --> 26:57.324
I got my hands on it,

26:58.074 --> 26:59.743
but I can't seem to open it.

27:00.994 --> 27:02.245
Mr. Eom Tae-seong.

27:04.456 --> 27:06.082
Did you take my trunk?

27:07.000 --> 27:08.335
I guess I did.

27:09.711 --> 27:11.004
But what to do?

27:13.048 --> 27:16.593
Should I expose the contract in this trunk
to the world…

27:19.012 --> 27:20.263
or kill Han Jeong-won first?

27:21.306 --> 27:22.849
Option one or two. Take your pick.

27:24.351 --> 27:25.685
My contract's over.

27:26.686 --> 27:28.813
I have nothing to do with him now.

27:29.481 --> 27:30.315
Why?

27:30.940 --> 27:32.025
Was it because of me?

27:36.946 --> 27:39.366
I think I'll kill Han Jeong-won first.

27:41.368 --> 27:43.703
I told you that the contract's over.

27:43.787 --> 27:47.040
It's not over yet. This never happened
in any of your other marriages.

27:47.123 --> 27:49.584
I've seen all your marriages,
dutiful yet without love.

27:49.668 --> 27:52.295
Things were going well.
You kept things professional!

27:53.463 --> 27:58.301
That's why I'm pissed off at Han Jeong-won
and that fucked up company of yours!

27:59.678 --> 28:02.931
It seems that company's trying
to get me committed again,

28:03.014 --> 28:05.016
or maybe they'll just kill me this time.

28:07.310 --> 28:08.645
Now it's come to this.

28:09.688 --> 28:12.691
Don't you think I need
a little insurance for myself?

28:13.775 --> 28:16.444
Let's meet.
I'll tell you the lock combinations.

28:21.658 --> 28:23.243
Where should we meet this time?

28:55.400 --> 28:58.486
Seo-yeon.

28:58.570 --> 28:59.571
Lee Seo-yeon!

29:01.406 --> 29:04.743
Gastric lavage.
Run a blood test, and call the police.

29:05.577 --> 29:06.786
Wake up, Lee Seo-yeon.

29:07.328 --> 29:10.206
Wake up, Lee Seo-yeon! Seo-yeon, please.

29:18.715 --> 29:20.008
So it's come to this.

29:22.844 --> 29:23.970
Are you happy now?

29:27.515 --> 29:29.684
She's always been a ticking time bomb.

29:33.646 --> 29:35.231
She wants to go home with you.

29:40.111 --> 29:41.571
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

29:41.654 --> 29:42.781
If I take her with me,

29:42.864 --> 29:45.325
she could OD and end up back here
to prove a point to you.

29:48.286 --> 29:49.704
Would you be okay with that?

30:05.720 --> 30:07.931
I know you won't listen
if I try to stop you…

30:10.767 --> 30:13.144
so go ahead and see it through to the end.

30:14.729 --> 30:15.563
I'm sorry.

30:20.109 --> 30:22.862
Don't call me. I'm going to be busy today.

31:00.525 --> 31:02.235
I thought I'd be comfortable here.

31:03.027 --> 31:04.445
You can use the first-floor bedroom.

31:10.410 --> 31:12.370
Acting like a child
will only wear you down.

31:12.453 --> 31:13.538
We're even, remember?

31:18.418 --> 31:21.421
I let you back into this house
so you could have some time.

31:23.339 --> 31:25.091
Time to face reality.

31:25.633 --> 31:28.094
I wondered why I couldn't leave you,

31:28.177 --> 31:30.638
but I've come to realize
it's because I pitied you.

31:33.057 --> 31:33.975
Seo-yeon,

31:35.143 --> 31:37.103
we can never go back
to the way things were.

31:38.062 --> 31:39.063
Neither of us.

32:13.598 --> 32:16.434
Are you really going?
What will you do all by yourself?

32:16.935 --> 32:19.228
I'll head over right now.
Tell me where you are.

32:20.688 --> 32:24.359
Si-jeong, I think I was the one
who did everything wrong.

32:25.526 --> 32:26.611
What do you mean?

32:27.654 --> 32:29.489
I was always to blame.

32:30.990 --> 32:33.451
For what happened to Hye-yeong, Do-ha,

32:34.827 --> 32:35.870
and Han Jeong-won.

32:37.455 --> 32:39.749
Why would you be to blame?

32:40.792 --> 32:43.044
Hey, In-ji?

32:43.127 --> 32:44.671
Are you there? In-ji!

33:00.478 --> 33:02.438
NOH IN-JI

33:04.565 --> 33:08.820
The person you have called
is currently unavailable. Please leave…

33:09.988 --> 33:11.781
NOH IN-JI

33:15.576 --> 33:17.495
HAN JEONG-WON

33:57.368 --> 33:59.746
You really came here alone.
How fearless of you.

34:00.830 --> 34:02.498
Should I be fearful?

34:02.582 --> 34:03.916
No, not you, Ms. In-ji.

34:06.085 --> 34:08.087
- I'll tell you the code.
- Wait.

34:08.713 --> 34:11.841
What's the rush? We just got here.

34:14.844 --> 34:17.680
The marriage contract and manual
are both in here, right?

34:18.264 --> 34:19.140
All the evidence.

34:26.814 --> 34:28.274
Why that look on your face?

34:29.025 --> 34:31.569
Afraid you'll end up like Seo Do-ha
once I open this?

34:31.652 --> 34:34.322
Are you scared
that people might point fingers at you?

34:34.864 --> 34:38.826
You seem to be taking pleasure
in my misfortune, Mr. Eom Tae-seong.

34:39.869 --> 34:42.789
Making you miserable publicly
would be ideal.

34:42.872 --> 34:44.999
That way, I'll be all you have left.

34:51.506 --> 34:54.634
You saw for yourself back then
what it's like.

34:55.259 --> 34:57.303
And what do you get out of this?

34:58.679 --> 35:01.224
Do you want to stay by my side
and share my misery?

35:05.603 --> 35:07.480
We can still turn this around.

35:08.231 --> 35:09.982
Go live your life.

35:11.109 --> 35:13.903
If you do that,
I'll forget any of this ever happened.

35:14.695 --> 35:15.613
The thing is…

35:17.573 --> 35:19.492
I wouldn't be miserable.

35:21.661 --> 35:24.580
What has your misery got to do with me?

35:24.664 --> 35:27.250
I'd just be by your side forever.

35:30.503 --> 35:32.046
That would be me living my life.

35:37.969 --> 35:40.555
I killed this pharmacist recently…

35:40.638 --> 35:42.515
I told you I killed someone, right?

35:43.808 --> 35:45.393
It's easier than you'd think.

35:46.310 --> 35:49.272
The cops still have no idea it was me.

36:04.537 --> 36:07.456
I'm kayaking in the moonlight
with Ms. In-ji. Care to join?

36:09.333 --> 36:10.501
Crazy bastard.

36:11.085 --> 36:12.044
NOH IN-JI

36:15.047 --> 36:17.800
The person you have called
is currently unavailable.

36:38.738 --> 36:39.906
What's wrong?

36:41.240 --> 36:43.784
Where did you get this from?

36:43.868 --> 36:45.995
Where do you think? Han Jeong-won's house.

36:46.787 --> 36:47.705
The dressing room.

36:59.800 --> 37:00.801
What is it?

37:04.055 --> 37:08.809
The lock must have jammed
because you tried to force it open.

37:11.437 --> 37:13.064
No way.

37:15.316 --> 37:18.194
You've got to be fucking kidding me!

37:20.029 --> 37:23.282
I can fix this if I take it to a store.
Come with me tomorrow.

37:26.619 --> 37:28.454
Do you think I'm a fucking idiot?

37:31.582 --> 37:33.042
What do you expect me to do?

37:33.834 --> 37:35.711
You should've come to me from the start.

37:35.795 --> 37:38.798
You should've come to me
instead of doing something so stupid!

37:43.010 --> 37:44.971
God-fucking-damn it!

37:49.642 --> 37:51.102
For fuck's sake.

38:04.907 --> 38:07.535
Will you stop all this nonsense
if I disappear?

38:14.166 --> 38:15.251
Mr. Eom Tae-seong.

38:17.253 --> 38:18.963
Let's just die together.

38:21.465 --> 38:23.175
Isn't that a tempting offer?

38:29.223 --> 38:30.182
Well, fuck me.

38:31.392 --> 38:34.979
Your jokes have gotten a lot better.
You almost had me with that one.

38:36.731 --> 38:39.400
But we can't die today.

38:42.945 --> 38:44.238
Option two comes first.

38:45.948 --> 38:46.782
"Option two"?

39:07.053 --> 39:09.472
Ms. In-ji!

39:10.681 --> 39:15.478
If I kill someone,
they'll just send me back to the hospital.

39:16.020 --> 39:16.854
Ms. In-ji!

39:17.563 --> 39:20.608
Why the hell are you doing this? Why?

39:21.567 --> 39:22.693
Just because.

39:22.777 --> 39:24.945
I'm doing this because I can.

39:26.072 --> 39:26.947
Ms. In-ji!

39:32.036 --> 39:33.037
Ms. In-ji.

39:33.120 --> 39:35.748
- Are you okay?
- Don't come closer, Mr. Han.

39:47.593 --> 39:48.677
Die!

40:39.645 --> 40:42.273
It's over. You can stop now.

40:42.356 --> 40:43.357
I shot him.

40:44.108 --> 40:46.735
I swear I shot him.

40:48.362 --> 40:51.615
It's okay.
What matters is that you're safe.

41:19.894 --> 41:20.811
You're okay.

42:12.071 --> 42:13.948
I thought they were live rounds.

42:24.959 --> 42:28.128
I was worried I might use them myself.

42:33.008 --> 42:34.343
Maybe I should have.

42:37.972 --> 42:39.431
I should've just killed him.

42:43.561 --> 42:44.895
Why would you do that?

42:45.479 --> 42:46.730
This is my problem.

42:51.026 --> 42:53.779
Don't go assuming that I did this for you.

42:54.613 --> 42:56.031
That wasn't the case.

42:58.701 --> 43:01.036
I can keep us both safe.

43:02.413 --> 43:03.372
That's good.

43:05.040 --> 43:07.501
Then go ahead and keep yourself safe.

43:09.753 --> 43:11.255
I'll do the same for myself now.

43:12.298 --> 43:13.132
Ms. In-ji…

43:17.970 --> 43:19.138
I just want this all to stop.

43:23.559 --> 43:24.393
I've…

43:26.437 --> 43:27.896
grown tired of it all.

44:22.368 --> 44:25.621
So you fired blanks in self-defense?

44:27.206 --> 44:28.832
Even if it were in self-defense,

44:28.916 --> 44:32.836
you know you'll still be punished
for possessing an illegal weapon, right?

44:35.214 --> 44:36.048
Yes.

44:45.557 --> 44:49.103
Who do you think killed Eom Tae-seong?

45:17.172 --> 45:18.173
Damn it.

46:24.156 --> 46:25.157
I keep thinking

46:25.657 --> 46:27.951
that you're the perfect person
for the job, Ji-o.

46:31.830 --> 46:35.125
Do you think
you could take care of Eom Tae-seong?

47:01.568 --> 47:03.445
I'll admit it. You were right.

47:04.655 --> 47:06.281
This marriage is what suits me.

47:07.616 --> 47:08.992
I'm saying you won.

47:31.181 --> 47:32.766
This shouldn't be like this.

47:34.935 --> 47:36.103
You…

47:37.354 --> 47:38.981
Where were you before you got here?

47:41.567 --> 47:42.734
I just…

47:46.613 --> 47:48.031
killed someone.

47:53.078 --> 47:54.705
I used to be a keeper for NM.

48:01.753 --> 48:04.798
I was there
when Eom Tae-seong killed my colleague…

48:07.175 --> 48:08.468
but I fled.

48:09.803 --> 48:12.180
It's bothered me ever since.

48:15.350 --> 48:16.977
But that wasn't the only reason.

48:27.613 --> 48:29.197
I quite liked this marriage.

48:35.704 --> 48:37.539
I'll move out as soon as I'm packed.

49:05.901 --> 49:09.488
Why did Eom Tae-seong have your trunk,
Ms. Lee Seo-yeon?

49:10.238 --> 49:11.198
Who knows?

49:11.823 --> 49:14.409
I never used that trunk
because it was hard to open.

49:14.493 --> 49:17.079
So you left it
at Mr. Han Jeong-won's house?

49:17.955 --> 49:19.206
I guess I must have.

49:27.255 --> 49:31.009
He was killed by a single stab
from a very long, sharp weapon.

49:39.142 --> 49:40.852
What might fit such a description?

49:42.729 --> 49:46.608
If it were at a construction site,
it could have been a sharp rebar stake.

49:46.692 --> 49:47.526
No.

49:48.527 --> 49:50.445
It was a sharp, smooth weapon.

49:52.406 --> 49:53.782
Aren't those fairly common?

49:57.619 --> 50:00.247
I don't get why
you're asking me such a thing.

50:09.297 --> 50:11.717
If there are no further questions,
can I go home?

50:11.800 --> 50:12.843
I'm rather tired.

50:14.886 --> 50:16.888
We've already gone over the contents.

50:16.972 --> 50:19.599
You should also check
that nothing's missing.

50:19.683 --> 50:21.518
It would put us in a tight spot

50:21.601 --> 50:23.770
if you later were to claim
something was missing.

51:25.916 --> 51:27.250
The realtor says

51:27.751 --> 51:30.796
it's a buyer's market,
so they had to lower the price.

51:33.423 --> 51:36.760
Please take good care of them.
I'm sure you've grown attached.

51:38.345 --> 51:40.472
And try to cut back on the coffee.

51:41.431 --> 51:44.101
Mind your own business
and just worry about yourself.

51:48.730 --> 51:49.564
What's wrong?

51:50.148 --> 51:52.150
All that's left for you
is to live happily with him.

51:55.153 --> 51:55.987
Am I wrong?

51:57.405 --> 52:00.075
I wish you the best of luck
with your next field wife.

52:03.078 --> 52:05.622
I knew you knew all along.

52:06.206 --> 52:07.290
You sure are something.

52:08.792 --> 52:09.793
You're just the worst.

52:10.293 --> 52:14.798
I should have told you about it sooner
instead of letting it weigh on me.

52:16.967 --> 52:17.884
I'll be going now.

52:22.973 --> 52:24.891
"This too shall pass," you know.

52:26.059 --> 52:27.686
Marriage isn't all it's cracked up to be.

52:28.311 --> 52:30.564
I've been divorced three times.
I should know.

53:11.313 --> 53:12.731
Is that all of your stuff?

53:14.191 --> 53:16.318
A trunk is all you need for a marriage.

53:26.703 --> 53:29.664
I wonder why it never crossed my mind
to leave this place.

53:31.666 --> 53:32.667
Was I afraid?

53:33.793 --> 53:34.836
Probably just lazy.

53:38.256 --> 53:40.258
Only the diligent bother moving.

53:41.509 --> 53:43.011
You need to fight landlords,

53:44.012 --> 53:45.847
buy new fridges and dining tables,

53:45.931 --> 53:48.350
and even find the perfect curtains.

53:52.354 --> 53:54.022
I'm not the lazy one here.

53:55.440 --> 53:59.986
If I were you, I'd have moved out
of that house a very long time ago.

54:03.031 --> 54:03.865
Unlikely.

54:07.369 --> 54:09.996
Are you really going
to tear this place down?

54:10.872 --> 54:11.706
Why?

54:12.832 --> 54:15.669
My delicate upbringing
prevents me from standing up to landlords.

54:16.628 --> 54:18.922
I'll grow lazy
and want to crawl back here.

54:19.005 --> 54:22.259
I need to remove the problem at its roots
so I can never return.

54:40.735 --> 54:42.279
You'll be demolishing it anyway.

54:42.362 --> 54:43.405
Join me.

55:27.657 --> 55:28.992
What were you going to say

55:30.702 --> 55:31.995
after "If I were you"?

55:33.246 --> 55:36.374
Was this it?
Me never returning to this house?

55:39.669 --> 55:41.004
Are you doing all this

55:42.297 --> 55:43.798
because of what I said?

55:45.884 --> 55:47.302
Isn't this what you meant?

55:49.679 --> 55:50.764
I was thinking…

55:56.519 --> 55:58.021
I would have rented it out…

56:00.690 --> 56:01.649
this place.

56:04.694 --> 56:07.864
I meant that I would travel abroad
with the rent money I'd earn.

56:08.990 --> 56:10.950
I didn't think
you'd do something like this.

56:12.369 --> 56:14.662
Rent out the place. Right.

56:23.296 --> 56:24.839
If we ever meet again…

56:28.468 --> 56:30.345
would you stay with me?

56:32.680 --> 56:36.101
Who knows?
We might be destined to be together.

56:37.852 --> 56:41.523
Maybe not for our entire lives,
but for around 30 years, perhaps.

56:48.405 --> 56:50.657
What if we run into each other
a second time?

56:54.702 --> 56:56.913
There's no helping it if it happens twice.

57:00.500 --> 57:01.626
So the second time.

57:03.336 --> 57:04.546
The second time it is.

57:12.929 --> 57:14.889
Thank you for everything,
Mr. Han Jeong-won.

57:20.895 --> 57:23.356
I wanted to tell you that, no matter what.

58:11.196 --> 58:15.825
DEAD BODY DISCOVERED AT LAKE
MURDER SUSPECT TAKEN INTO CUSTODY

58:36.221 --> 58:38.181
Hello, Attorney Choi.

58:39.349 --> 58:40.767
I have a case for you.

58:55.698 --> 58:58.201
Ms. Yoon-a called me here
to check out the remodeling.

58:58.785 --> 59:00.119
You don't need to explain.

59:00.787 --> 59:03.915
I know, but I find myself explaining.

59:07.669 --> 59:11.923
I'm re-signing my contract with Ji-o.
I'll also hire him the best lawyer I can.

59:17.679 --> 59:18.513
Seo-yeon.

59:22.141 --> 59:24.394
I once thought
that you were not letting me go,

59:26.145 --> 59:27.105
but in reality…

59:29.107 --> 59:30.858
I wasn't letting you go.

59:32.277 --> 59:36.072
I owed you a proper explanation
as to why we couldn't work.

59:39.325 --> 59:40.451
I'm just a bad person.

59:41.494 --> 59:43.162
That's how I've found my closure.

59:44.497 --> 59:46.499
Believing it hurts my pride less.

01:00:28.207 --> 01:00:30.543
Momo. Hey, Momo?

01:00:31.628 --> 01:00:32.712
Sleepy, are we?

01:00:35.423 --> 01:00:36.424
Hey there, Cookie.

01:01:30.228 --> 01:01:31.354
I'm so lonely.

01:01:53.376 --> 01:01:59.716
ITERATION

01:02:17.984 --> 01:02:20.903
DIRECTED BY NOH SU-HWAN
SCREENPLAY BY YANG JEONG-WON

01:02:28.828 --> 01:02:30.580
MUSIC BY HAN JEONG-WON

01:02:56.355 --> 01:02:57.440
What is it?

01:02:57.523 --> 01:03:01.194
The movie released
after a ten-month delay,

01:03:01.277 --> 01:03:02.612
but the reviews are lukewarm.

01:03:03.237 --> 01:03:06.783
Then again, who goes to the cinema
to watch horror B-movies nowadays?

01:03:08.659 --> 01:03:11.954
I know you're not fishing,
so stop moping and come to the office.

01:03:12.038 --> 01:03:13.706
I said I'm not at a fishing spot.

01:03:13.790 --> 01:03:16.709
Just hurry back.
I think my wife's going to divorce me.

01:03:18.252 --> 01:03:19.253
It's not that bad.

01:03:27.637 --> 01:03:30.014
- What did you say this was?
- A file for divorce.

01:03:30.723 --> 01:03:32.391
These days, I fill one out daily.

01:03:32.892 --> 01:03:33.726
Why?

01:03:33.810 --> 01:03:36.938
It's the only place I can be alone
without you and the kids.

01:03:37.021 --> 01:03:38.147
"The only place"?

01:03:38.231 --> 01:03:40.691
You hog our bathroom
because you're constipated.

01:03:42.068 --> 01:03:43.361
I have no place of my own.

01:03:43.444 --> 01:03:46.072
But you've got a name and title.
Director Oh Hyeon-cheol.

01:03:46.656 --> 01:03:51.118
You even have your own office,
while I'm just a mother and wife.

01:03:52.620 --> 01:03:55.706
You know I'm the only one of my friends
who's married, right?

01:03:56.207 --> 01:03:58.918
They're all living it up as they please,

01:03:59.001 --> 01:04:00.586
but I've achieved nothing.

01:04:01.295 --> 01:04:04.966
I understand that one of us
needs to take care of the kids.

01:04:08.761 --> 01:04:09.846
I get that, but…

01:04:14.642 --> 01:04:18.354
I don't think it makes me very happy.

01:04:22.817 --> 01:04:23.985
Go see a dermatologist.

01:04:24.652 --> 01:04:27.530
Get a laser facial.
I'll give you my personal card.

01:04:27.613 --> 01:04:30.199
Why can't we ever have
a serious conversation?

01:04:30.992 --> 01:04:32.827
Can't we at least do that?

01:04:33.536 --> 01:04:35.830
3,000 won? Seriously?

01:04:36.706 --> 01:04:38.332
I can give you more.

01:04:39.041 --> 01:04:40.459
No, it's fine. That will do.

01:04:41.168 --> 01:04:43.504
You're an odd one,
turning down a better offer.

01:04:44.839 --> 01:04:46.257
Did you use it to store a corpse?

01:04:48.301 --> 01:04:49.969
Just kidding, of course.

01:04:51.846 --> 01:04:54.181
- Have a nice day.
- Thanks, you too.

01:04:55.558 --> 01:04:57.476
This really is a beauty.

01:04:59.687 --> 01:05:02.023
I wonder what I should use it for.

01:05:03.482 --> 01:05:05.443
It's got such a lovely design.

01:05:18.205 --> 01:05:20.958
AMERICANO - 3,000 WON

01:05:29.216 --> 01:05:30.801
Enjoy.

01:05:30.885 --> 01:05:32.136
Thank you.

01:07:45.436 --> 01:07:47.521
I was visiting a vet here.

01:07:48.773 --> 01:07:50.399
My cat's claw fell out.

01:07:52.234 --> 01:07:54.653
I have cats now, by the way.

01:07:56.113 --> 01:07:56.947
Right.

01:08:00.326 --> 01:08:01.202
Have you been well?

01:08:05.956 --> 01:08:07.416
It was scary, by the way.

01:08:09.710 --> 01:08:11.545
I saw the movie.

01:08:14.298 --> 01:08:16.050
Did you see the end credits?

01:08:18.344 --> 01:08:19.762
That's why I went.

01:08:29.897 --> 01:08:31.232
This is the first one.

01:08:34.568 --> 01:08:36.362
Our first chance encounter.

01:08:45.204 --> 01:08:47.039
One more to go.

01:08:49.625 --> 01:08:50.459
Yes.

01:11:16.522 --> 01:11:19.733
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
